# Metric Widget — 5 design suggestions

The Metric widget today renders one hero number (`count` / `sum` / `avg` of
matching instances), an optional `delta` vs 7d/30d ago, a `format`
(plain/compact/currency/percent), and two layouts (`tile` vertical, `bar`
horizontal). Below are 5 distinct visual treatments to grow it. Each notes
what existing config drives it and what *new* config it would need.

---

## 1 · Hero Tile  *(refined default)*

Single big number, caption, delta line. Number scales to tile height.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│                              │
│                              │
│     1,284                    │
│     Open Deals               │
│     ▲ +112 vs 30d ago        │
│                              │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

Drives from: `agg` + `field` → number · `label` → caption · `delta` → arrow line.
New config: none — this is the current `variant:"tile"`, just the baseline.

---

## 2 · Stat Bar  *(dense header strip)*

Short + wide tiles collapse to one line: number, label, delta pill on the
right. Great for a row of KPIs across the top of a dashboard.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  $4.2M   Pipeline value              ▲ +8.3%    │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Drives from: current `variant:"bar"` (auto-picks on short/wide tiles).
New config: `delta` could render as % pill instead of raw `+N`.

---

## 3 · Sparkline KPI  *(number + inline trend)*

Hero number with a tiny sparkline of the value over the delta window, so the
trend is visible at a glance — not just a single before/after diff.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  New Signups            7d ▾  │
│                              │
│  342          ▁▂▃▅▆▇█        │
│  ▲ +24%                      │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

Drives from: `agg`/`field` → number · `delta` window → sparkline span.
New config: `variant:"spark"` + a `series` bucket (day/week) for the trail.

---

## 4 · Delta Spotlight  *(now vs then)*

Inverts the emphasis: the *change* is the headline. Big % delta, with the
current and baseline values shown small underneath.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  Active Customers            │
│                              │
│    ▲ +6.4%                   │
│    910   ·   was 855 (30d)   │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

Drives from: `delta` (required here) · `agg`/`field` → both endpoints.
New config: `variant:"delta"` · `format:"percent"` on the change itself.

---

## 5 · Gauge Ring  *(value as proportional fill)*

Radial ring filling toward a reference (a percent metric, or value/target).
Reads as "how far along" rather than an absolute count.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│         ╭───────╮            │
│        ╱  72%    ╲           │
│       │ ███████   │          │
│        ╲ on-track ╱          │
│         ╰───────╯            │
│      Win rate                │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

Drives from: `format:"percent"` value → fill fraction.
New config: `variant:"gauge"` + optional `target` (overlaps Goal widget —
decide whether Metric grows a ring or this stays Goal's job).

---

## At a glance

| # | Variant   | Headline       | New config needed                 |
|---|-----------|----------------|-----------------------------------|
| 1 | Hero Tile | the number     | none (current)                    |
| 2 | Stat Bar  | number + delta | delta-as-% pill (optional)        |
| 3 | Sparkline | number + trend | `variant:"spark"` + series bucket |
| 4 | Spotlight | the change     | `variant:"delta"`                 |
| 5 | Gauge     | progress       | `variant:"gauge"` (+ target?)     |

Suggest building 1–2 first (cheap, no schema change), then 3/4 as new
`variant` literals on the existing widget. 5 overlaps Goal — needs a call.
